verses.text:
34. Flee from such men as much as you can;
avoid with a wholesome caution those who adhere to their mischievous
contact. Their word doth eat as doth a cancer;
[2 Tim. ii. 17.]

be wanting;
but, moreover, that vengeance, which should defend with heavenly
defence those who were hurt, should attend them.

This
is differently read “a widow, a poor widow is found,” etc.;
or, “a woman widowed and poor.”

33. That the Father judgeth nothing, but the Son;
and the Father is not honoured by him by whom the Son is not
honoured.

“Say not, I will avenge me of mine enemy;
but wait for the Lord, that He may be thy help.”
Lev. xix. 18.
